                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f7abdf75-49c1-3f7e-b19b-55b0e62c6ec4",
                        "entry_id": "3b102b68-384b-309b-bcdd-3beae7bca216",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui vit sur la terre ou dans la terre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e88feaa-16d1-4218-b340-ef5af44661f1",
                                "sense_id": "f7abdf75-49c1-3f7e-b19b-55b0e62c6ec4",
                                "text": "La Cystolépiote de Bucknal est un saprophyte terricole que l’on trouve dans les lisières, sur les banquettes des haies forestières et sur les bermes de routes. Ce taxon acidocline et nitrophile pourrait être plus répandu que ne le montre notre carte. Sa répartition semble cantonnée à l’étage collinéen dans le Nord-Est."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "745f5ba1-4935-4c05-8731-425bc8406c4b",
                        "source_entry_id": "3b102b68-384b-309b-bcdd-3beae7bca216",
                        "source_sense_id": "f7abdf75-49c1-3f7e-b19b-55b0e62c6ec4",
                        "target_lang_word": "terricole",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "terricole",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0589c6cf-3b27-3358-8862-37ac40388198",
                                        "entry_id": "f76279d6-49a5-3c8c-a7f6-1b2a94b64786",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ground-dwelling or growing close to the ground."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a439ea44-e1eb-435c-997f-73d4f8cd37a5",
                                                "sense_id": "0589c6cf-3b27-3358-8862-37ac40388198",
                                                "text": "Man himself is terricole in habits, with vertical carriage, and walking on two feet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1111def6-ea12-4dea-89df-d73eb149ecdd",
                                                "sense_id": "0589c6cf-3b27-3358-8862-37ac40388198",
                                                "text": "The plant from Heald Brow is terricole, occurring on loose sandy calcareous earth about the entrances to rabbit-holes, in a very dry locality, Heald Brow being a dry hill on the scar-limestone."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bae1f566-ad84-4d33-b12c-981b318e2dec",
                                                "sense_id": "0589c6cf-3b27-3358-8862-37ac40388198",
                                                "text": "The greatest bulk of the typical high altitude insects are generally small-sized, flightless or apterous, mostly heavily pigmented, terricole forms that occur under stoness, in the immediate vicinity of glaciers, snow and melt waters."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d25a46e-1e58-4add-ab2b-e79a5368599d",
                                                "sense_id": "0589c6cf-3b27-3358-8862-37ac40388198",
                                                "text": "These peculiarities depend largely on the moisture requirements of the terricole species. In humid weather, the top layer of the soil is usually highly saturated and moist, so that the terricole species generally occur on the upper layers of the soil."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "terricole",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "198a4f5c-3006-36b3-b032-33b6187bf2da",
                                        "entry_id": "b2cb6d40-91ba-3bfd-a79f-a37497ad4f36",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any insect that lives on or in the ground, especially one that is flightless."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cfb133ea-5172-4426-b1b0-3c53d048c1ba",
                                                "sense_id": "198a4f5c-3006-36b3-b032-33b6187bf2da",
                                                "text": "The Terricoles are the true Crane Flies, seen in damp meadows in great numbers, especially in the autumn."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebf2f933-fdfc-4a47-a3f6-4e0101bf069b",
                                                "sense_id": "198a4f5c-3006-36b3-b032-33b6187bf2da",
                                                "text": "Still another subdivision of terricoles consists of species of high alpine habitats with scanty and very short vegetation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6e13cdf-ee47-48f1-8e00-d063faa39b32",
                                                "sense_id": "198a4f5c-3006-36b3-b032-33b6187bf2da",
                                                "text": "Two types of grasshoppers are common in desert grasslands: terricoles, or soil mimics (the color pattern matches soil or rocks), and graminicoles, or grass mimics (the color pattern matches grass leaves)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
